The Edit facility on Journal Entries was already fully built (form,
mutation, submit handling) but never appeared: the frontend checked
entry.type === 'MANUAL' while the API actually returns the field as
source (confirmed against DayBookPage, which reads it correctly).
undefined === 'MANUAL' is always false, so the button never rendered
for any entry, Manual or Auto.

Also hardened the server side to match: updateEntry only checked that
debits equal credits, with no guard against editing an Auto-posted
entry (which would desync it from whatever created it — a dues
payment, expense, or provision), a cancelled entry, or an entry in a
closed financial year. Added all three, mirroring the same checks
attachDocument already applies to the same entity.

